    "description": "LiveOak Fiber is a regional broadband provider building and operating fiber-to-the-premises networks in the southeastern United States. Its customers include residential households and businesses in historically underinvested communities that require high-speed broadband connectivity. The operating model is asset-heavy and recurring because the company invests in last-mile fiber infrastructure and generates subscription revenues from connected premises. Public materials state that LiveOak was founded in 2022, has invested more than $200 million, built over 1,000 miles of fiber, and serves markets in Florida and Georgia. InfraRed committed initial growth capital in 2022 and partnered with MEAG in a 2024 co-investment, while the current ownership percentages were not publicly disclosed.",
